{"title":"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sixty meters of rope is used to make three sides of a rectangular camping area with a long wall used as the other side. The length of each side of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Natural_number\" title=\"Natural number\">natural number</a>. What is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum\" title=\"Maximum\">largest</a> area that can be enclosed by the rope and the wall? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the side <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> to the wall, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> adjacent to the wall. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/6/e6642eb5c725912fc87d0ce67ad71c02bb27e961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l + 2w = 60 \\Longrightarrow l = 60 - 2w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"225\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e259652d34a747895e7e66007135a0138307a1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$lw = -2w^2 + 60w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />; this is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">quadratic equation</a>, which we can maximize using the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/c/69ce163c720cbcf2b3e11363d7b529b131251582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-b}{2a} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" />. Hence the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/60479500264fbcafa49ac7bca7875a0a31c19a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2(15)^2 + 60(15) = 450$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC\" title=\"2005 PMWC\">2005 PMWC </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I12\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I12\">Problem I12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_PMWC_Problems/Problem_I14\" title=\"2005 PMWC Problems/Problem I14\">Problem I14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\">I: <a href=\"/wiki/index.p